{"Title":"An Act relative to the visibility of fire hydrants","BillNumber":"S1594","DocketNumber":"SD2352","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"BET0","Name":"Bruce E. Tarr","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/BET0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-20T16:11:11.793"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"BET0","Name":"Bruce E. Tarr","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/BET0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-20T16:11:11.7933333"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S1594/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Mr. Tarr, a petition (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 1594) of Bruce E. Tarr for legislation relative to the visibility of fire hydrants.  Public Safety and Homeland Security.","DocumentText":"\tChapter 148 of the General Laws is hereby amended by inserting after section 27B the following section:- \r\n\tSection 27C. Fire hydrant visibility\r\n\tFire hydrants installed in the commonwealth or any political subdivision thereof located in any public or private way shall be painted in colors that maximize their visibility, contrast with their surroundings, and do not include the color white unless used as a secondary color to contrast with the surroundings of the area. \r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Favorable","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J22","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J22"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}